.\" Manpage for CannonBall SE
.TH "cannonball-se" "6" "September 2026" "CannonBall SE 1.50" "CannonBall SE Configuration Help"
.SH OVERVIEW
\fBCannonBall-SE\fP is a fork of Chris White's incredible cross-platform OutRun engine optimised for home-brew arcade cabinets.
It adds enhanced image processing to provide an authentic CRT look, MP3 playback, and performance optimisations.

.SH OPTIONS
Command line options:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
-h                  : Displays the command-line options and man page link, then quits
.IP \(bu 2
-list-audio-devices : Lists available playback devices, then quits
(\fB-list-sound-devices\fP is accepted as a synonym)
.IP \(bu 2
-cfgfile            : Set the location and name of config.xml
.IP \(bu 2
-file               : LayOut Editor track data to load (for custom routes)
.IP \(bu 2
-30 or -60          : Force 30 or 60fps operation (disables auto frame rate selection)
.IP \(bu 2
-t [1-4], eg -t 1   : Override hardware thread detection and use specified number of threads (1-4)
.IP \(bu 2
-x                  : Disable single-core RaspberryPi board detection
.IP \(bu 2
-1                  : Use single-core mode (game will run in one thread, plus sound)
.IP \(bu 2
-perftest           : Measure the maximum frame rate this machine can sustain, then quit.
Use this to check whether your board has headroom for a heavier shader or hi-res mode.
.RE
.PP
Additional development and diagnostic options exist; run \fB-h\fP to list them.

.SH GETTING STARTED
The following assumes that the game was downloaded and built in your home directory as ~/cannonball-se.
.PP
To run cannonball, copies of the original arcade ROMs are needed (more info in the ROMs section below) - copy these to ~/cannonball-se/roms before proceeding.
.PP
To start the game, "cd ~/cannonball-se" then "build/cannonball-se".

.SH CONTROLS
The default keyboard controls are:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Start Game (in free-play mode)                   - S
.IP \(bu 2
Coin In (starts game when not in-free play mode) - C
.IP \(bu 2
Accelerate                                       - A
.IP \(bu 2
Brake                                            - Z
.IP \(bu 2
Select Low Gear                                  - G
.IP \(bu 2
Select High Gear                                 - H
.IP \(bu 2
Steer Left/Right                                 - Left/Right Arrows
.IP \(bu 2
Change View                                      - V
.IP \(bu 2
Menu                                             - M
.IP \(bu 2
Up/down (in menu)                                - Up/Down Arrows
.IP \(bu 2
Select option or change value in menu            - S
.IP \(bu 2
Quit Game (Master Break Key)                     - Escape
.RE
.PP
These can also be changed within the game (menu, settings, controls, redefine keys) and the master break key (Escape) can be changed to F10 in Menu, Settings.
.PP
The function keys are fixed and cannot be redefined:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
F1  - Pause
.IP \(bu 2
F2  - Frame step (while paused)
.IP \(bu 2
F3  - Toggle game timer
.IP \(bu 2
F5  - Open menu
.IP \(bu 2
F7  - Toggle hi-res sprites
.IP \(bu 2
F8  - Toggle all video processing on/off
.IP \(bu 2
F9  - Toggle shadow mask
.RE
.PP
See \fIdocs/PLAYING.md\fP for full control and configuration details.

.SH STEERING WHEELS
Steering wheels, joysticks and gamepads can be setup in the game (menu, settings, controls, configure inputs).
.PP
Configure Inputs auto-detects axis direction during capture (the "turn wheel left" prompt for steering, and similar for the pedals), so an inverted wheel or pedal needs no manual invert setting.

.SH ROMS
CannonBall needs a copy of the OutRun 'revision B' romset to function. These should be copied to the roms subdirectory
(usually ~/cannonball-se/roms). Please see the file roms.txt for file names and other information.
.PP
Instead of loose files, a MAME-format ROM archive (e.g. a merged or split outrun.zip) may be placed in the
roms directory unextracted, since ROMs inside it are matched by content rather than filename; loose files
in the roms directory always take priority over an archive. See \fIroms.txt\fP for the full list of
accepted archive names and where else they are searched for.
.PP
\fBIMPORTANT:\fP Users of CannonBall (and CannonBall-SE) are expected to own licensed copies of the original arcade ROMs that
are needed for the program to function. The use of ROM images may be restricted by copyright or other laws depending on jurisdiction.
The end-user assumes all responsibility in respect of the use of original ROMs.

.SH CUSTOM MUSIC
.PP
CannonBall-SE supports custom music via .WAV and .MP3 files placed in the \fIres\fP directory and named
[01-99]_Track_Display_Name.[wav|mp3] - e.g. 04_AHA_Take_On_Me.mp3. Indexes 01-03 replace the built-in
tracks and 04 and higher add tracks to the radio screen list; files should be 44.1kHz, 16-bit stereo.
See \fIdocs/PLAYING.md\fP for full detail.

.SH FUNCTIONALITY
.PP
On top of the game port provided by CannonBall, CannonBall-SE provides:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Video-processing enhancements - NTSC filter, screen curvature, analogue noise, shadow mask, and bezel mask.
.IP \(bu 2
Enhanced audio module for consistent, pop-free audio and custom music via MP3 playback.
.IP \(bu 2
Enhanced rumble support for compatible steering wheels (rumbles on tyre smoke).
.IP \(bu 2
Performance enhancements and automatic frame rate selection.
.IP \(bu 2
Play count and 'machine hours' tracking (menu, about).
.IP \(bu 2
Various stability and bug fixes.
.RE

.SH CHOOSING A PLATFORM
.PP
Cannonball-SE runs on Raspberry Pi boards with Raspberry Pi OS, and on Intel/AMD PCs with Ubuntu. Every quad-core Pi reaches
60fps at 1280x1024, though Pi 2 and Pi 3 class boards may need the fast shader or a small GPU clock bump to do so; single-core
boards run at 30fps. A CPU heatsink is recommended on multi-core Pis.
.PP
Run \fBcannonball-se -perftest\fP to measure what your own board sustains; see \fIdocs/PERFORMANCE-TUNING.md\fP for the full
board-by-board guide.

.SH STUTTERING AUDIO
.PP
If audio stutters, try switching the sound callback interval to 16MS (Menu/Settings/Sound/Audio Callback Interval - AUTO
already resolves to this on Pi 1/2/3), and prefer HDMI audio, which is handled by the GPU. See \fIdocs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md\fP
for USB-audio and video-driver specifics.

.SH WATCHDOG SUPPORT
.PP
On systems with a hardware watchdog (including all Raspberry Pi boards), CannonBall-SE hooks this so the system is
automatically rebooted if a hang occurs, for example due to aggressive overclocking.

.SH APPLIANCE MODE
.PP
On Raspberry Pi OS, \fBinstall.sh\fP can optionally set the machine up as a dedicated appliance that boots straight into the
game with a splash screen and powers off when you quit. Other consoles (Ctrl+Alt+F2 and so on) and SSH remain available
throughout. It is fully reversible with \fB./install.sh --remove-appliance\fP; see \fIdocs/INSTALL.md\fP for details.

